{"id": "EUVD-2026-68918", "enisaUuid": "376a9e13-8fd6-335e-89c5-d8e4a7c2bc01", "description": "A flaw was found in popt. This vulnerability allows an attacker to provide specially crafted configuration content to a host, which, when loaded, can lead to a small memory corruption issue. This occurs because of an error in how the `poptConfigFileToString` function reallocates memory for buffers. Successful exploitation could result in heap metadata corruption, potentially causing the affected process to become unavailable (denial of service).", "datePublished": "2026-09-01T00:57:12", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-08T22:53:46", "baseScore": 2.5, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:H/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:L", "references": ["https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:56984", "https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-18743", "https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2510809"], "aliases": ["GHSA-2r56-6h49-5c5r", "CVE-2026-18743"], "assigner": "redhat", "epss": 0.14, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0b6ac99c-bd7e-3a8c-804e-c490b64806e9", "product": {"name": "popt", "vendor": {"name": "rpm-software-management"}}, "product_version": "1.11 <*"}, {"id": "4ee461de-61f8-3ffe-90e8-7d49f1ed84e9", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Hardened Images", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 1.19-11.1.hum1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "83907467-93a3-3f84-a6ac-65ddc815cee6", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, {"id": "cf4f5fbf-83a3-3903-98b3-753d7b5a1351", "vendor": {"name": "rpm-software-management"}}], "isExploited": false}